{
  "_comment": [
    "J6 target calibration records: one per measured target, each the evidence a frozen",
    "EncodingCostTable was built from. bcir/asn1/calibration.py decides admissibility;",
    "tools/silicon/measure_asn1_calibration.sh produces a record on a declared target.",
    "",
    "Every record must carry the same `corpus` digest: two targets that measured different",
    "schemas produce two tables that look identical, compare cleanly, and mean nothing.",
    "",
    "steal_ticks/throttled_usec are null on Android, where /proc/stat is restricted. Null",
    "means UNREPORTED, not zero -- the reader declines to refuse on a counter nobody could",
    "read, rather than treating an unchecked counter as evidence the declaration held."
